ized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4150079327","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73XTZV","author":{"login":"sungdark"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-03-29T12:37:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4150081109","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73XXBN","author":{"login":"wallidsaydi-creator"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-03-29T12:47:33Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4150095949","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73Xba7","author":{"login":"sungdark"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"我来认领！收款地址：eB51DWp1uECrLZRLsE2cnyZUzfRWvzUzaJzkatTpQV9","createdAt":"2026-03-29T12:58:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4150113979","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73Xcro","author":{"login":"zhaog100"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt","createdAt":"2026-03-29T13:01:56Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4150119144","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73YQ6V","author":{"login":"denaev-dev"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt","createdAt":"2026-03-29T15:04:15Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4150333077","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73Y9-Q","author":{"login":"guidou2013-bot"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-03-29T16:38:53Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4150517648","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73bqUW","author":{"login":"sungdark"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"我来认领！\n\n收款地址：eB51DWp1uECrLZRLsE2cnyZUzfRWvzUzaJzkatTpQV9","createdAt":"2026-03-29T22:33:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4151223574","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73b89g","author":{"login":"rhyk7"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nThe hardest part here isn't the content — it's making Claude skip the \"what database client are you using?\" clarification loop, which means the CLAUDE.md needs explicit better-sqlite3/Turso decision points, migration file naming patterns (e.g., `0001_create_users.sql`), and App Router conventions like co-locating server actions with their route segments. I'll structure it around the four sections that eliminate ambiguity: stack pinning, folder layout, DB rules, and a \"we don't do X\" list with explicit reasoning. I can have a PR ready within 2 days.","createdAt":"2026-03-29T23:22:57Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4151299936","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73chhj","author":{"login":"guidou2013-bot"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\n---\n\nHi! I'm Guillaume Micallef, a developer who builds SaaS products and AI-powered tools. I use Next.js App Router + SQLite in production and have strong opinions about how a project like this should be set up â€” which is exactly what this bounty calls for.\n\nI've written a **complete, opinionated CLAUDE.md** for a Next.js 15 + SQLite SaaS. Every rule has a reason. Nothing is generic.\n\n---\n\n## What I Built\n\nA production-ready `CLAUDE.md` covering all required sections plus several I added because they matter:\n\n### Sections included\n\n| Section | What it covers |\n|---|---|\n| **Stack & Versions** | Next.js 15, React 19, TypeScript 5 strict, better-sqlite3, Drizzle ORM, Tailwind 4, Zod, Auth, Testing â€” with a \"Why\" column for every choice |\n| **Folder Structure** | Complete annotated tree: route groups, server/ boundary, lib/db/, components/ui vs features, types/ â€” with rules on what can import what |\n| **DB & Migration Conventions** | Schema patterns (CUID2 IDs, integer timestamps, soft deletes), Drizzle migration workflow, query rules (keyset pagination not OFFSET, no raw SQL in route handlers) |\n| **Component Patterns** | Server Components by default, \"use client\" checklist, data fetching patterns, Server Actions with Zod validation pattern |\n| **Dev Commands** | All scripts mapped to npm run aliases with what they do |\n| **What We Don't Do** | 10 explicit anti-patterns with alternatives and reasons â€” this is the section that makes Claude stop doing dumb things |\n| **Environment Variables** | Required vars with examples |\n| **TypeScript Rules** | strict mode, no @ts-ignore policy, Drizzle type inference |\n| **Testing Philosophy** | What to unit test vs integration test vs E2E, and what NOT to test |\n| **Git Conventions** | Branch naming, commit style, merge strategy |\n\n---\n\n## Sample from the CLAUDE.md\n\n**The \"What We Don't Do\" section** (this is where most CLAUDE.md templates fail â€” they tell Claude what to do but not what to avoid):\n\n| We don't do this | We do this instead | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| `pages/` directory | `app/` directory | We're on Next.js 15 App Router â€” no mixing |\n| UUID primary keys | CUID2 | Shorter, URL-safe, time-sortable |\n| `OFFSET` pagination | Cursor-based (keyset) | OFFSET degrades at scale |\n| Hard delete | Soft delete (`deletedAt`) | User data is precious; hard deletes are irreversible |\n| `any` type | Drizzle inferred types + Zod | Type safety is the entire point |\n| Business logic in components | `server/actions/` and `server/queries/` | Components render; servers compute |\n\n**The schema pattern section** (gives Claude the exact template to follow every time it creates a table):\n\n```ts\nexport const users = sqliteTable(\"users\", {\n  id:        text(\"id\").primaryKey(),           // CUID2, generated at app level\n  email:     text(\"email\").notNull().unique(),\n  createdAt: integer(\"created_at\", { mode: \"timestamp\" }).notNull().default(sql`(unixepoch())`),\n  updatedAt: integer(\"updated_at\", { mode: \"timestamp\" }).notNull().default(sql`(unixepoch())`),\n});\n```\n\n**Server Action pattern** (so Claude never writes business logic in route handlers again):\n\n```ts\n\"use server\"\nexport async function updateUser(formData: FormData) {\n  const parsed = updateUserSchema.safeParse(Object.fromEntries(formData));\n  if (!parsed.success) return { error: parsed.error.flatten() };\n  await db.update(users).set(parsed.data).where(eq(users.id, parsed.data.id));\n  revalidatePath(\"/dashboard\");\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Why this CLAUDE.md works without clarifying questions\n\nThe key is specificity. Generic CLAUDE.mds say things like \"follow best practices.\" This one says:\n\n- \"Use CUID2, not UUID, not auto-increment integers\"\n- \"Paginate with `limit` + `cursor` (keyset), not OFFSET\"\n- \"Never write raw SQL in route handlers â€” always go through `server/queries/`\"\n- \"Return `{ error }` or `{ data }` from Server Actions â€” never throw\"\n\nClaude doesn't need to ask what \"best practices\" means when it has the exact pattern in front of it.\n\n---\n\nHappy to adjust anything based on feedback!\n\nâ€” Guillaume Micallef (@guillaumemcf)\n","createdAt":"2026-03-30T00:31:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4151449699","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73dAp5","author":{"login":"clawctrl1"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"I would like to claim this bounty. I will create a production-ready CLAUDE.md template for Next.js + SQLite SaaS projects.","createdAt":"2026-03-30T01:25:57Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4151577209","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73f8Gq","author":{"login":"zhaog100"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/attempt","createdAt":"2026-03-30T05:32:30Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4152345002","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73mxhv","author":{"login":"geldbert"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-03-30T11:03:42Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4154136687","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73nIyW","author":{"login":"RavMonSOL"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-03-30T11:20:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4154231958","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M73ntZK","author":{"login":"geldbert"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-03-30T11:39:4