e-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/724) - opinionated, production-ready CLAUDE.md. Covers all required sections. Ready for merge.","createdAt":"2026-05-01T06:01:52Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4358074018","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABA8bBow","author":{"login":"wbobbynmworley"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Our PR is ready: [PR #724](https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/724)\n\n**Why our solution stands out:**\n\n- Covers ALL required sections from issue description\n- Includes naming conventions table (pages, components, server actions, DB tables, API routes)\n- SQL migration conventions with parameterized query examples\n- Transaction patterns with better-sqlite3\n- Server vs Client component rules\n- React Hook Form + Zod everywhere\n- Anti-patterns table (what we don't do and why)\n- Dev commands, API response pattern, 5-paragraph structure\n","createdAt":"2026-05-01T07:26:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4358324643","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBA_0Ig","author":{"login":"vantaq-labs"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-02T06:10:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4363121698","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBBEkjA","author":{"login":"yihangwu539-png"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire claim\n\nPR: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/687","createdAt":"2026-05-02T06:43:17Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4363199628","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBE_HjQ","author":{"login":"abhayjnayakk"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-03T22:14:23Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4367304589","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBOPMPA","author":{"login":"chatgptbot517-netizen"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"This submission introduces a comprehensive CLAUDE.md configuration tailored for modern SaaS architectures using Next.js 15 and SQLite. It provides clear, opinionated guidelines for server-side data fetching, Drizzle ORM patterns, and secure Server Actions. This template is designed to streamline development for any team utilizing AI-assisted coding tools in this specific stack.\n\n# CLAUDE.md - Next.js 15 + SQLite SaaS\n\n> Production-ready context guide for Claude Code working on a Next.js 15 App Router + SQLite SaaS project.\n\n## Stack & Versions\n\n```\nNext.js: 15.x (App Router)\nSQLite: better-sqlite3 or @local-first/sync (Turso compatible)\nRuntime: Node.js 20+\nPackage Manager: npm (no pnpm/yarn)\nStyling: Tailwind CSS\nAuth: NextAuth.js v5 with credentials or OAuth\nDeployment: Vercel or Railway\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\n/\n|-- app/                      # Next.js App Router pages\n|   |-- (auth)/             # Auth routes (login, register, forgot)\n|   |-- (dashboard)/        # Protected dashboard routes\n|   |-- api/                # API Route Handlers\n|   |   |-- auth/           # NextAuth endpoints\n|   |   |-- [resource]/     # RESTful resource handlers\n|   |-- layout.tsx\n|-- components/\n|   |-- ui/                 # Shadcn/ui primitives only\n|   |-- forms/              # React Hook Form + Zod schemas\n|   |-- features/            # Feature-specific components\n|-- lib/\n|   |-- db/                 # Database client + migrations\n|   |   |-- client.ts       # better-sqlite3 instance\n|   |   |-- migrations/     # SQL migration files\n|   |-- auth/               # Auth utilities\n|   |-- utils.ts            # Shared helpers\n|-- scripts/                 # DB seed / migrate scripts\n|-- CLAUDE.md               # <- You are here\n```\n\n**Key rule**: Never put business logic in app/api/*.ts directly. Always go through lib/ modules.\n\n## Naming Conventions\n\n| Thing | Convention | Example |\n|-------|------------|---------|\n| Pages | kebab-case | app/users/page.tsx |\n| Components | PascalCase | UserCard.tsx |\n| Server actions | camelCase | createUser() |\n| Database tables | snake_case | user_accounts |\n| API routes | kebab-case | app/api/user-profile/route.ts |\n| CSS classes | Tailwind only | className=\"text-lg font-medium\" |\n\n## SQL / Migration Conventions\n\n### Migrations\n\n1. All schema changes via migration files in lib/db/migrations/\n2. 2. Naming: 0001_add_users.sql, 0002_add_sessions.sql, etc.\n3. 3. **Never run DROP or ALTER in production migrations** - only additive changes\n4. 4. Use better-sqlite3's synchronous API for server components; async for API routes\n### Query Patterns\n\n```typescript\n// V DO: Use parameterized queries, never string interpolation\nconst user = db.prepare('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?').get(userId)\n\n// X DON'T: String interpolation allows SQL injection\nconst user = db.prepare(`SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ${userId}`).get()\n```\n\n### Transactions\n\n```typescript\n// Wrap multi-step operations in transactions\nconst result = db.transaction(() => {\n  const user = db.prepare('INSERT INTO users ...').run(...);\n  db.prepare('INSERT INTO sessions ...').run(...);\n  return user;\n})();\n```\n\n## Component Patterns\n\n### Server vs Client Components\n\n- app/ files with use client = interactive UI only\n- - Everything else = Server Component by default\n- - - **Never** fetch data in client components - use Server Components + fetch() with cache\n### Form Handling\n\n```typescript\n// V DO: React Hook Form + Zod everywhere\nconst schema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  password: z.string().min(8),\n});\nconst form = useForm<z.infer<typeof schema>>({ resolver: zodResolver(schema) });\n\n// X DON'T: useState for form state\n// X DON'T: uncontrolled inputs for anything beyond trivial forms\n```\n\n### Feature Components\n\nEach feature gets its own folder under components/features/:\n\n```\ncomponents/features/users/\n|-- UserList.tsx         # Server Component (fetches data)\n|-- UserListClient.tsx   # Client wrapper for interactivity\n|-- UserCard.tsx\n|-- index.ts            # Re-exports\n|-- UserForm.tsx        # If needed\n```\n\n## What We Don't Do (and Why)\n\n| Pattern | Why We Avoid It |\n|---------|----------------|\n| Class components | React Server Components + functional only |\n| useEffect for data fetching | Server Components + actions instead |\n| Inline styles | Tailwind only, consistent design system |\n| npm run dev in production | Use proper deployment (Vercel/Railway) |\n| Storing secrets in code | Environment variables via .env.local |\n| console.log in production | Use structured logging to stdout |\n| Direct db.exec() in API routes | Use typed db.prepare() with parameterization |\n\n## Dev Commands\n\n```bash\nnpm run dev          # Start development server (http://localhost:3000)\nnpm run db:migrate   # Run pending migrations\nnpm run db:seed      # Seed development database\nnpm run build        # Production build\nnpm run lint         # ESLint check\nnpm run type-check   # tsc --noEmit\n```\n\n## API Response Pattern\n\nAll API routes return this shape:\n\n```typescript\n// app/api/example/route.ts\nexport async function GET(request: Request) {\n  try {\n    const data = await getExampleData();\n    return Response.json({ ok: true, data });\n  } catch (error) {\n    return Response.json(\n      { ok: false, error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unknown error' },\n      { status: 400 }\n    );\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Anti-Patterns to Flag\n\nIf Claude Code tries any of these, redirect immediately:\n\n- X \"use server\" in component files (put it in lib/actions/)\n- - X JSON.parse() on untrusted input\n- - - X Storing plain-text passwords (must be hashed with bcrypt/argon2)\n- - - - X Returning raw database rows as API responses (always validate + transform)\n- - - - - X any type annotations (use unknown + type guards instead)\n- - - - - ","createdAt":"2026-05-05T06:34:11Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4377005116","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBOY_cA","author":{"login":"chatgptbot517-netizen"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-05T07:03:48Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4377165680","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBOnfWA","author":{"login":"mengyuyuan"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-05T07:45:06Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4377403224","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBPvkMQ","author":{"login":"chengyixu"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-05T10:55:44Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4378584113","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBRb6dg","author":{"login":"mengyuyuan"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nI just spent the day building and deploying a Next.js 16 + Prisma + SQLite production app. I'll write an opinionated CLAUDE.md covering:\n- Project structure & naming conventions\n- SQL/migration rules with Prisma\n- Server/Client component patterns\n- Anti-patterns we learned the hard way\n- Dev commands & workflows\n\nEach rule backed by real production experience.","createdAt":"2026-05-05T14:43:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4380359286","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBfWIoA","author":{"login":"Ace-Ronin"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nI will submit a production-ready CLAUDE.md for Next.js 15 + SQLite SaaS. PR coming shortly.","createdAt":"2026-05-07T07:12:42Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4394944672","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBjH8wg","author":{"login":"mert-kocoglu"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-07T16:17:06Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4398906562","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBkhZLA","author":{"login":"zkksdk"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-07T19:22:51Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4400372012","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBngc2Q","author":{"login":"litvinov-tech"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-08T05:07:27Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4403502297","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBqNtDw","author":{"login":"benjamenhoffman"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-08T12:19:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4406340879","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBtgEsA","author":{"login":"litvinov-tech"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"PR submitted: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/774\n\nCLAUDE.md template for Next.js 15 App Router + SQLite SaaS projects.\n\nPayout address: `0xdF7E9D6640BEcA1239276D4aA72E53321619E1c1`","createdAt":"2026-05-08T20:55:45Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4409787568","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBv8VWg","author":{"login":"zeropclab"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-09T10:52:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4412347738","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBwBjTg","author":{"login":"borjamoskv"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-09T11:40:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4412433230","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBwDzOw","author":{"login":"tjgarcia0427"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-09T12:01:44Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4412470075","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBwE7sg","author":{"login":"Freeman88-tch"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-09T12:12:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4412488626","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBwF8NA","author":{"login":"Freeman88-tch"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"CyGqoMi8SA39YYvkmdiZmY3LbjUJMSTQVRymwpBR5QBy","createdAt":"2026-05-09T12:21:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4412505140","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBxsBiw","author":{"login":"litvinov-tech"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Taking this bounty. PR #774 is submitted with a production-oriented Next.js 15 + SQLite CLAUDE.md template and the setup guidance covered.","createdAt":"2026-05-10T01:48:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4414177675","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBx5rsA","author":{"login":"zhaog100"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"我来认领这个任务！\n\n**我的方案：**\n- 完整的 Next.js 15 + SQLite (better-sqlite3) SaaS CLAUDE.md 模板\n- 包含：项目结构、命名规范、数据库迁移规则\n- 包含：开发命令、遵循的模式、避免的反模式\n- 包含：组件模式、SQL约定、迁移规范\n\n**付款地址 (TRC20 USDT):** TGu4W5T6q4KvLAbmXmZSRpUBNRCxr2aFTP","createdAt":"2026-05-10T04:10:08Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4414401456","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABByKPhg","author":{"login":"leoop8563"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\n","createdAt":"2026-05-10T06:56:30Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4414672774","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBybDEw","author":{"login":"saurabh224s"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-10T09:27:19Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4414948115","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBydyjg","author":{"login":"saurabh224s"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"## Create the CLAUDE.md File\n\n1. In your file explorer, go to `Desktop/claude-builders-bounty/`\n2. Right-click → **New → Text Document** → name it `CLAUDE.md`\n3. Open it in any text editor (Notepad, VS Code, etc.)\n4. Paste the content I'll provide below\n5. Save the file\n\n---\n\n##  Create a New Branch & Commit\n\nIn Terminal/Command Prompt (make sure you're in the `claude-builders-bounty` folder):\n\n```bash\n# Create a new branch\ngit checkout -b add-claude-md\n\n# Add your file\ngit add CLAUDE.md\n\n# Commit (save) with a message\ngit commit -m \"Add CLAUDE.md for Next.js + SQLite SaaS project\"\n```\n\n---\n\n##  Push to GitHub\n\n```bash\ngit push origin add-claude-md\n```\n\n---\n\n## Create a Pull Request (PR)\n\n1. Go to **your fork** on GitHub: `github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/claude-builders-bounty`\n2. You'll see a yellow banner: **\"add-claude-md had recent pushes\"** → click **\"Compare & pull request\"**\n3. Add a title: `Add CLAUDE.md for Next.js + SQLite SaaS bounty`\n4. In the description, mention: `Closes #2`\n5. Click **\"Create pull request\"**\n\n---\n\n\n\n## 📝 Here's the CLAUDE.md Content to Paste\n\nCopy and paste this into your `CLAUDE.md` file:\n\n```markdown\n# CLAUDE.md — Next.js 15 + SQLite SaaS\n\n## Stack & Versions\n\n- **Next.js 15** (App Router, Server Components by default)\n- **React 19** (RC or stable)\n- **TypeScript 5** (strict mode enabled)\n- **Tailwind CSS 4** (utility-first, no arbitrary values in production)\n- **better-sqlite3** (local SQLite) OR **@libsql/client** (Turso/cloud)\n- **Drizzle ORM** (preferred over raw SQL for type safety)\n- **Zod** (runtime validation, always validate at API boundary)\n- **NextAuth.js v5** (Auth.js) or **Lucia** (if rolling custom auth)\n\n> **Why this stack:** SQLite is sufficient for 95% of SaaS apps until 100k+ users. \n> Drizzle gives type-safe SQL without the Prisma black box. Next.js 15 App Router \n> eliminates API boilerplate via Server Actions.\n\n---\n\n## Folder Structure\n\n```\nmy-saas/\n├── app/                    # Next.js App Router\n│   ├── (auth)/             # Route groups (no URL segment)\n│   │   ├── login/\n│   │   └── register/\n│   ├── (dashboard)/        # Authenticated routes\n│   │   ├── layout.tsx      # Auth guard + sidebar\n│   │   ├── page.tsx        # Dashboard home\n│   │   └── settings/\n│   ├── api/                # Route handlers (rarely needed)\n│   ├── layout.tsx          # Root layout (providers, fonts)\n│   └── globals.css\n├── components/\n│   ├── ui/                 # shadcn/ui components (never edit directly)\n│   ├── forms/              # Form-specific components\n│   └── features/           # Domain-specific (e.g., BillingTable)\n├── lib/\n│   ├── db/                 # Database layer\n│   │   ├── schema.ts       # Drizzle schema (single source of truth)\n│   │   ├── migrations/     # Generated by drizzle-kit\n│   │   └── index.ts        # DB client singleton\n│   ├── auth.ts             # Auth configuration\n│   └── utils.ts            # cn() helper, general utilities\n├── hooks/                  # Custom React hooks\n├── types/                  # Global TypeScript types (rarely needed)\n└── public/                 # Static assets\n```\n\n> **Why:** Route groups keep URLs clean while co-locating related pages. \n> The `lib/db/` directory is the ONLY place SQL lives. No queries in components.\n\n---\n\n## SQL / Migration Conventions\n\n### Schema Rules\n1. **Single file:** All tables in `lib/db/schema.ts`\n2. **Naming:** `snake_case` for DB columns, `camelCase` in TypeScript (Drizzle maps them)\n3. **Timestamps:** Every table gets `created_at` and `updated_at` (use `defaultNow()`)\n4. **Soft deletes:** Use `deleted_at` (nullable timestamp) instead of `DELETE` for user data\n5. **Foreign keys:** Always define with `onDelete: 'cascade'` or `'set null'` explicitly\n6. **Indexes:** Add indexes on every foreign key and frequently queried column\n\n### Migration Workflow\n```bash\n# 1. Modify schema.ts\n# 2. Generate migration\nnpx drizzle-kit generate\n\n# 3. Review the generated SQL in migrations/ folder\n# 4. Apply to local DB\nnpx drizzle-kit migrate\n\n# 5. For Turso production\nnpx drizzle-kit push:sqlite   # or turso specific command\n```\n\n> **Why:** Reviewing generated SQL catches Drizzle bugs. Never hand-write migrations \n> unless fixing a broken one. Soft deletes prevent accidental data loss and simplify GDPR.\n\n---\n\n## Component Patterns\n\n### Server Components (Default)\n```tsx\n// app/(dashboard)/page.tsx\nimport { db } from '@/lib/db'\nimport { users } from '@/lib/db/schema'\n\nexport default async function DashboardPage() {\n  // ✅ Query directly in Server Component\n  const allUsers = await db.select().from(users)\n  \n  return <UserTable data={allUsers} />\n}\n```\n\n### Client Components (Only when needed)\n```tsx\n'use client'\n\n// Use ONLY for:\n// - Interactivity (onClick, useState, useEffect)\n// - Browser APIs (localStorage, clipboard)\n// - Real-time features (WebSockets)\n\nimport { useState } from 'react'\n\nexport function Counter() {\n  const [count, setCount] = useState(0)\n  return <button onClick={() => setCount(c => c + 1)}>{count}</button>\n}\n```\n\n### Server Actions\n```tsx\n// app/(dashboard)/actions.ts\n'use server'\n\nimport { db } from '@/lib/db'\nimport { users } from '@/lib/db/schema'\nimport { revalidatePath } from 'next/cache'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nconst createUserSchema = z.object({\n  email: z.string().email(),\n  name: z.string().min(1),\n})\n\nexport async function createUser(formData: FormData) {\n  // ✅ Validate at the boundary\n  const data = createUserSchema.parse({\n    email: formData.get('email'),\n    name: formData.get('name'),\n  })\n  \n  await db.insert(users).values(data)\n  \n  // ✅ Revalidate to refresh Server Component data\n  revalidatePath('/dashboard')\n}\n```\n\n> **Why:** Server Components reduce client JS by 70%+. Server Actions replace \n> API routes for mutations, eliminating serialization boilerplate. Always validate \n> with Zod — never trust client input.\n\n---\n\n## Dev Commands\n\n```bash\n# Install dependencies\nnpm install\n\n# Run dev server (Turbopack recommended)\nnpm run dev\n\n# Type check (run before every commit)\nnpx tsc --noEmit\n\n# Lint\nnpm run lint\n\n# DB operations\nnpx drizzle-kit generate    # Generate migration\nnpx drizzle-kit migrate     # Run migrations locally\nnpx drizzle-kit studio      # Open Drizzle Studio (GUI for DB)\n\n# Build for production\nnpm run build\n\n# Start production build locally\nnpm start\n```\n\n---\n\n## What We Don't Do (And Why)\n\n| Don't | Why |\n|-------|-----|\n| ❌ Use `useEffect` to fetch data on mount | Use Server Components or Server Actions instead. Eliminates loading states, race conditions, and hydration mismatches. |\n| ❌ Put SQL queries in `.tsx` files outside `lib/db/` | Database logic must be centralized. Components should call functions, not write SQL. |\n| ❌ Use `any` type | Disables TypeScript's value. Use `unknown` + narrowing if types are unclear. |\n| ❌ Store secrets in `.env.local` only | Use `.env.local` for local dev, but verify production secrets are in Vercel/Turso dashboard. |\n| ❌ Use `SELECT *` | Always select specific columns. Prevents breaking changes when adding columns. |\n| ❌ Skip migrations and use `push` in production | `drizzle-kit push` can drop data. Migrations are versioned and reviewable. |\n| ❌ Use `use client` at the top of every file | Default to Server Components. Only 10-20% of components need to be client-side. |\n| ❌ Handle auth in every page manually | Use route group layouts `(dashboard)/layout.tsx` with auth guards. |\n| ❌ Use raw SQL without Drizzle | Only acceptable in migrations or complex queries. Drizzle provides type safety and prevents SQL injection. |\n| ❌ Commit `.env` files | Add `.env*.local` to `.gitignore`. Leaked secrets are irreversible. |\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start (Greenfield Project)\n\n```bash\n# 1. Create project\nnpx create-next-app@latest my-saas --typescript --tailwind --app\n\n# 2. Install stack\ncd my-saas\nnpm install drizzle-orm better-sqlite3\nnpm install -D drizzle-kit @types/better-sqlite3\n\n# 3. Copy this CLAUDE.md to project root\n# 4. Create lib/db/schema.ts with your first table\n# 5. Run: npx drizzle-kit generate && npx drizzle-kit migrate\n# 6. Start building in app/(dashboard)/\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing the Context\n\nAfter pasting this CLAUDE.md into a project, Claude Code should be able to:\n\n1. Generate a new table in `lib/db/schema.ts` with proper conventions\n2. Create a Server Component that queries the DB without asking about fetch patterns\n3. Write a Server Action with Zod validation without clarifying where it should go\n4. Know to use `snake_case` for DB columns and `camelCase` in TS\n5. Prefer soft deletes over hard deletes\n6. Use route groups for auth vs. public layouts\n","createdAt":"2026-05-10T09:52:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4414993038","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBzwzLg","author":{"login":"DavideZanonArt"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-10T21:08:27Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4416353070","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBzx4_Q","author":{"login":"Emil-10"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-10T21:16:52Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4416370941","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBzyt9w","author":{"login":"gzmh2021"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"C:/Program Files/Git/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-10T21:23:27Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4416384503","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABBz0f5Q","author":{"login":"ScryUser"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-10T21:38:03Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4416413669","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABB0Df2w","author":{"login":"rovaro-crew"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-10T23:48:12Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4416659419","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABB0bCnQ","author":{"login":"Dewaldnel11"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-11T02:06:06Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4417045149","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABB0iEhg","author":{"login":"wptechprodigy"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-11T02:40:37Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4417160326","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABB0pd3A","author":{"login":"minyanyi"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try\n\nSubmitted PR: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/868","createdAt":"2026-05-11T03:12:47Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4417281500","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABB0rU-w","author":{"login":"agentjohnwalker007"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-11T03:22:04Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4417311995","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABB0u7mA","author":{"login":"mandarin77"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-11T03:33:17Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4417371032","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABB1Q4yg","author":{"login":"gok11"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-11T05:54:59Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4417927370","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABB2WeGg","author":{"login":"kaziiza"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-11T09:03:27Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4419067418","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABB2bCDg","author":{"login":"OMGletmein"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try","createdAt":"2026-05-11T09:12:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4419142158","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABB2jXTA","author":{"login":"alexgduarte"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"/opire try PR submitted: #900 - https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/900. Added an opinionated Next.js 15 + SQLite CLAUDE.md template with rule reasons, 3-step README setup, and a scratch Claude Code context check.","createdAt":"2026-05-11T09:29:22Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/issues/2#issuecomment-4419278668","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDORx6c0M8AAAABB2ltNw","author":{"login":"kaziiza"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"Submitted PR: https://github.com/claude-builders-bounty/claude-builders-bounty/pull/902","createdAt":"2026-05-11T09:34:52Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reacti